  "refinements": [
    "Four real release origins have distinct executor and result/error rules; wrapper invalidation/attempt is distinct from successful native destruction",
    "Device cleanup can unlink before close failure, wait using implicit processor OS state, and free device storage after a virtual-release error; no universal retry-on-error policy",
    "Nine admission obligations cover identity, complete effects, executor, lock progress, code/input custody, failure, phase reservation, origin semantics and shutdown",
    "Memory epoch completion differs from native release drain; retained-unknown diagnostic does not return custody pins or establish resource closure",
    "One necessary DeviceReleaseCoordinator has ten source registration expressions using one existing shared callback; no ten-fold shared-body savings",
    "Modern C credits existing helper/generation/failure funnel; new generation has real costs, as does Zig comptime/tooling. Eight support obligations, five retirement conditions and six economic countermodels retain unresolved positive bounds"
  ],
